WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:32.041
<b>Lord Krishna says here,</b>

2
00:00:32.041 --> 00:00:33.083
<b>O Arjuna,</b>

3
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:36.083
<b>Without attachment to any kind of fruit,</b>

4
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:41.208
<b>you should perform your actions, </b>
<b>considering it merely as a sacrificial offering.</b>

5
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:44.750
<b>Only such action can liberate you</b>
<b>from the bondage of karma.</b>

6
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.500
<b>The action which is not performed in this way</b>

7
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.875
<b>will not be able to free one from bondage.</b>

8
00:00:54.708 --> 00:00:57.333
<b>Arjuna has expressed this fear earlier also,</b>

9
00:00:57.333 --> 00:01:01.166
<b>that if he fights the war and his loved ones die,</b>

10
00:01:01.166 --> 00:01:03.708
<b>then the sin of this will be on his head.</b>

11
00:01:03.708 --> 00:01:07.875
<b>To free Arjuna from this very fear, </b>
<b>Krishna is explaining here.</b>

12
00:01:07.875 --> 00:01:09.083
<b>He is saying that</b>

13
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:12.625
<b>to be free from the</b>
<b>karmic bondage of sin and virtue</b>

14
00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:18.833
<b>- perform your actions, without attachment to </b>
<b>the fruits, considering it merely as a sacrifice.</b>

15
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:20.541
<b>Let’s understand this</b>

16
00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:23.208
<b>- this fact is extremely important.</b>

17
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:27.833
<b>According to Vedic scriptures, one of</b>
<b>the names of Lord Vishnu is also Yagya.</b>

18
00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:32.583
<b>This implies that whatever work</b>
<b>is being done for the Yagya,</b>

19
00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:35.708
<b>is being done only for Lord Vishnu.</b>

20
00:01:35.708 --> 00:01:36.291
<b> And</b>

21
00:01:36.291 --> 00:01:38.958
<b>that work which is performed </b>
<b>according to the Vedas</b>

22
00:01:38.958 --> 00:01:41.291
<b>and is dedicated to Lord Vishnu,</b>

23
00:01:41.291 --> 00:01:47.208
<b>only that can free a person from </b>
<b>karmic bondage i.e. sin and virtue.</b>

24
00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:48.333
<b>Apart from this,</b>

25
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:53.750
<b>sin or virtue is inevitably </b>
<b>incurred in any kind of work.</b>

26
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.750
<b>Lord Krishna wants to say</b>

27
00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.750
<b>- O Arjuna</b>

28
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.083
<b> - considering this war as a sacrifice, </b>

29
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:01.250
<b>perform it for Lord Vishnu.</b>

30
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.500
<b>Whatever the outcome, dedicate it to Him.</b>

31
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.250
<b>Consider that you are merely </b>
<b>an instrument of Lord Vishnu,</b>

32
00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.083
<b>through which He is getting all these actions done.</b>

33
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:16.625
<b>In this situation, you will not partake in any sin.</b>

34
00:02:16.625 --> 00:02:17.416
<b>Here,</b>

35
00:02:17.416 --> 00:02:20.333
<b>also understand the two meanings of Yagya.</b>

36
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:21.291
<b>The first is</b>

37
00:02:21.291 --> 00:02:23.625
<b>the general definition of Yagya –</b>

38
00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:27.666
<b>the offering of ghee and other materials in fire.</b>

39
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:31.791
<b>The fire of Yagya is considered to </b>
<b>be the tongue of Lord Vishnu.</b>

40
00:02:31.791 --> 00:02:36.916
<b>In this way, every material offered to </b>
<b>the fire is offered to Lord Vishnu.</b>

41
00:02:36.916 --> 00:02:41.958
<b>This is an expression of the gratitude of the </b>
<b>devotees and their being indebted to the Lord.</b>

42
00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:47.958
<b>The level mentioned in this verse </b>
<b>is even higher than selfless Karma Yoga.</b>

43
00:02:47.958 --> 00:02:50.708
<b>Where the meaning of selfless Karma Yoga</b>

44
00:02:50.708 --> 00:02:53.166
<b>is the renunciation of attachment to the fruit,</b>

45
00:02:53.166 --> 00:02:55.875
<b>here there is not only the renunciation </b>
<b>of that attachment,</b>

46
00:02:55.875 --> 00:03:03.125
<b>but also the dedication of every fruit arising</b>
<b>from the action at the feet of Lord Vishnu.</b>

47
00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:05.166
<b>Here the devotee is offering,</b>

48
00:03:05.166 --> 00:03:08.250
<b>and the Lord is accepting it.</b>

49
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.791
<b>This is indicative of the affection between </b>
<b>the devotee and the Lord.</b>

50
00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:18.875
<b>And it is this affection, this devotion </b>
<b>that makes the path to liberation even sweeter.</b>

51
00:03:18.875 --> 00:03:20.875
<b>Think about it.</b>

52
00:03:25.791 --> 00:03:27.958
<b>Selfless work,</b>

53
00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:31.916
<b>Action (Karma) performed without desire for fruit</b>

54
00:03:31.916 --> 00:03:36.291
<b>- man has started forgetting this principle.</b>

55
00:03:36.291 --> 00:03:39.458
<b>Even before the beginning of any work,</b>

56
00:03:39.458 --> 00:03:43.458
<b>the mind starts craving for the final goal.</b>

57
00:03:43.458 --> 00:03:46.041
<b>How much wealth will be gained in the end,</b>

58
00:03:46.041 --> 00:03:48.083
<b>how much fame will be earned,</b>

59
00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:54.000
<b>without thinking this, man does </b>
<b>not even start the work.</b>

60
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.250
<b>It's not that there is no need for wealth in life.</b>

61
00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.625
<b>There definitely is.</b>

62
00:04:00.625 --> 00:04:01.833
<b>But,</b>

63
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:05.583
<b>instead of considering wealth as an object of use,</b>

64
00:04:05.583 --> 00:04:09.750
<b>if man becomes a slave to wealth itself,</b>

65
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.333
<b>then how is this appropriate?</b>

66
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:15.958
<b>When man leaves action</b>

67
00:04:15.958 --> 00:04:19.541
<b>and starts craving only for the result,</b>

68
00:04:19.541 --> 00:04:27.666
<b>he gets stuck in an endless cycle </b>
<b>of enjoyment and luxury.</b>

69
00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:29.791
<b>Life does not remain joyful,</b>

70
00:04:29.791 --> 00:04:30.750
<b>but</b>

71
00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:36.333
<b>becomes a race chasing after wealth and greed.</b>

72
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:38.458
<b>Think for yourself</b>

73
00:04:38.458 --> 00:04:45.166
<b>- in the span of life, by now God knows </b>
<b>how many goals you would have achieved,</b>

74
00:04:45.166 --> 00:04:47.250
<b>every time thinking that</b>

75
00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:54.541
<b>if only this last goal is achieved </b>
<b>then the mind will find peace.</b>

76
00:04:54.541 --> 00:04:56.000
<b>But</b>

77
00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.750
<b>did this happen?</b>

78
00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.333
<b>No, right?</b>

79
00:04:59.333 --> 00:05:06.208
<b>After the achievement of every goal, the joy of </b>
<b>the mind did not last even for a moment,</b>

80
00:05:06.208 --> 00:05:08.291
<b>but,</b>

81
00:05:08.291 --> 00:05:15.416
<b>a new race for a new goal definitely started.</b>

82
00:05:15.416 --> 00:05:18.958
<b>If this kind of life is not bondage,</b>

83
00:05:18.958 --> 00:05:20.458
<b>then what is?</b>

84
00:05:20.458 --> 00:05:21.541
<b>But</b>

85
00:05:21.541 --> 00:05:29.666
<b>when a person enjoys only the action without </b>
<b>desiring the fruit, selflessly,</b>

86
00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:33.083
<b>then this is a very liberating experience.</b>

87
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:35.500
<b>Think</b>

88
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:41.291
<b>- life is such a journey, where you </b>
<b>cannot stay at any destination,</b>

89
00:05:41.291 --> 00:05:44.291
<b>you have to keep moving constantly.</b>

90
00:05:44.291 --> 00:05:49.083
<b>So in such a case, where should </b>
<b>happiness be sought?</b>

91
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:50.500
<b>In the destination?</b>

92
00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.541
<b>Or</b>

93
00:05:51.541 --> 00:05:52.708
<b>is it in the journey?</b>

94
00:05:52.708 --> 00:05:55.958
<b>It is the journey that is continuous</b>

95
00:05:55.958 --> 00:05:58.500
<b>- happiness will have to be sought in that.</b>

96
00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:02.375
<b>The destination is momentary.</b>

97
00:06:02.375 --> 00:06:04.958
<b>Craving for it is futile.</b>

98
00:06:04.958 --> 00:06:06.583
<b>Now</b>

99
00:06:06.583 --> 00:06:11.458
<b>take this a step further</b>

100
00:06:11.458 --> 00:06:19.041
<b>- when you are enjoying the action itself, </b>
<b>the worry of the fruit is not bothering you,</b>

101
00:06:19.041 --> 00:06:19.875
<b>and</b>

102
00:06:19.875 --> 00:06:25.375
<b>now you are doing this action</b>
<b>also for the welfare of others.</b>

103
00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:28.625
<b>Doing it for the society.</b>

104
00:06:28.625 --> 00:06:31.916
<b>How liberating will this experience be.</b>

105
00:06:31.916 --> 00:06:33.083
<b>Action (Karma),</b>

106
00:06:33.083 --> 00:06:34.875
<b>which gives joy.</b>

107
00:06:34.875 --> 00:06:35.958
<b>Action (Karma),</b>

108
00:06:35.958 --> 00:06:39.833
<b>from the craving of whose fruit you are free.</b>

109
00:06:39.833 --> 00:06:40.916
<b>Action (Karma),</b>

110
00:06:40.916 --> 00:06:46.875
<b>in which you see the good of others.</b>

111
00:06:46.875 --> 00:06:48.791
<b>Think about it.</b>

112
00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:56.291
<b>Everyone wants only this,</b>

113
00:06:56.291 --> 00:07:00.500
<b>that their loved ones remain happy.</b>

114
00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.000
<b>But,</b>

115
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.291
<b>have you ever thought</b>

116
00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:10.458
<b>what happiness truly is?</b>

117
00:07:10.458 --> 00:07:13.458
<b>How can it be attained?</b>

118
00:07:13.458 --> 00:07:14.958
<b>Imagine,</b>

119
00:07:14.958 --> 00:07:20.583
<b>- in a prison, a prisoner who is serving a sentence.</b>

120
00:07:20.583 --> 00:07:22.000
<b>For him,</b>

121
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.833
<b>happiness has only one meaning,</b>

122
00:07:24.833 --> 00:07:28.708
<b>freedom from that prison.</b>

123
00:07:28.708 --> 00:07:30.916
<b>His independence.</b>

124
00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:33.375
<b>Now think,</b>

125
00:07:33.375 --> 00:07:35.375
<b>Usually,</b>

126
00:07:35.375 --> 00:07:42.125
<b>man himself is also trying to be free from </b>
<b>bondage throughout life.</b>

127
00:07:42.125 --> 00:07:43.708
<b>Some youth</b>

128
00:07:43.708 --> 00:07:46.666
<b>wants to do a new job,</b>

129
00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:52.208
<b>so that he is not financially </b>
<b>dependent on his family,</b>

130
00:07:52.208 --> 00:07:54.625
<b>becomes free from bondage.</b>

131
00:07:54.625 --> 00:08:00.583
<b>Someone is trying to leave his job </b>
<b>and start a new business,</b>

132
00:08:00.583 --> 00:08:05.166
<b>so that he can be free from the cycle of job.</b>

133
00:08:05.166 --> 00:08:06.666
<b>Some businessman</b>

134
00:08:06.666 --> 00:08:09.583
<b>is earning wealth for this reason,</b>

135
00:08:09.583 --> 00:08:13.208
<b>so that he still has all the comforts,</b>

136
00:08:13.208 --> 00:08:19.125
<b>he is trying to be free from sorrows.</b>

137
00:08:19.125 --> 00:08:22.083
<b>Man is searching for this only,</b>

138
00:08:22.083 --> 00:08:23.500
<b>Freedom.</b>

139
00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:24.708
<b>Because</b>

140
00:08:24.708 --> 00:08:28.250
<b>there is happiness only in freedom.</b>

141
00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.916
<b>But</b>

142
00:08:29.916 --> 00:08:32.708
<b>the irony is only this,</b>

143
00:08:32.708 --> 00:08:36.625
<b>that man is searching for it in the wrong place.</b>

144
00:08:36.625 --> 00:08:38.791
<b>Think about it,</b>

145
00:08:38.791 --> 00:08:40.958
<b>who is happy?</b>

146
00:08:40.958 --> 00:08:43.583
<b>The one who asks for happiness,</b>

147
00:08:43.583 --> 00:08:48.125
<b>or the one who distributes happiness to others?</b>

148
00:08:48.125 --> 00:08:50.375
<b>Who is free?</b>

149
00:08:50.375 --> 00:08:53.208
<b>The one who is searching for freedom,</b>

150
00:08:53.208 --> 00:08:54.500
<b>or</b>

151
00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:57.208
<b>the one who is himself free,</b>

152
00:08:57.208 --> 00:08:58.333
<b>and</b>

153
00:08:58.333 --> 00:09:01.958
<b>is also showing the path to others.</b>

154
00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:06.166
<b>Happiness is only with the one who is free,</b>

155
00:09:06.166 --> 00:09:11.041
<b>and completely free is the one</b>

156
00:09:11.041 --> 00:09:13.750
<b>who is free from the bondage of Karma,</b>

157
00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:16.083
<b>who is not a slave to cravings,</b>

158
00:09:16.083 --> 00:09:17.916
<b>who does not ask,</b>

159
00:09:17.916 --> 00:09:21.583
<b>only gives to others.</b>

160
00:09:21.583 --> 00:09:27.208
<b>To act selflessly for the welfare of others.</b>

161
00:09:27.208 --> 00:09:30.500
<b>How liberating this thought is.</b>

162
00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.750
<b>Descend into this life,</b>

163
00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:33.666
<b>and</b>

164
00:09:33.666 --> 00:09:37.583
<b>also inspire your loved ones for this.</b>

165
00:09:37.583 --> 00:09:43.541
<b>They will also get a sense of </b>
<b>happiness and freedom.</b>

166
00:09:43.541 --> 00:09:44.708
<b>Think about it.</b>

167
00:09:49.625 --> 00:09:52.000
<b>Without an attachment to the fruit,</b>

168
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.833
<b>to keep performing actions,</b>

169
00:09:54.833 --> 00:09:57.583
<b>is selfless Karma Yoga. (Nishkam Karma Yoga).</b>

170
00:09:57.583 --> 00:09:58.541
<b>And</b>

171
00:09:58.541 --> 00:10:02.541
<b>to dedicate the result of the action </b>
<b>to the welfare of others,</b>

172
00:10:02.541 --> 00:10:05.625
<b>to the society,</b>

173
00:10:05.625 --> 00:10:07.958
<b>this is a Yagya,</b>

174
00:10:07.958 --> 00:10:11.625
<b>which can free one from the bondage of karma.</b>

175
00:10:11.625 --> 00:10:12.791
<b>Now</b>

176
00:10:12.791 --> 00:10:17.291
<b>this doubt may arise in professional life</b>

177
00:10:17.291 --> 00:10:21.125
<b>- that it is okay to seek joy only in action,</b>

178
00:10:21.125 --> 00:10:25.041
<b>it is okay to not have attachment to the fruit,</b>

179
00:10:25.041 --> 00:10:25.916
<b>but</b>

180
00:10:25.916 --> 00:10:28.000
<b>welfare of society?</b>

181
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:35.041
<b>Then should a person leave his designated </b>
<b>profession and start doing welfare of society,</b>

182
00:10:35.041 --> 00:10:37.958
<b>start doing only charity?</b>

183
00:10:37.958 --> 00:10:38.791
<b>Sin</b>

184
00:10:38.791 --> 00:10:39.583
<b>and virtue,</b>

185
00:10:39.583 --> 00:10:41.250
<b>welfare of society,</b>

186
00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:43.083
<b>good and bad deeds.</b>

187
00:10:43.083 --> 00:10:49.666
<b>The profound analysis of all these will </b>
<b>definitely come in further studies as well.</b>

188
00:10:49.666 --> 00:10:53.083
<b>But understand this here</b>

189
00:10:53.083 --> 00:10:58.708
<b>- that you can do welfare of society from </b>
<b>your current profession as well.</b>

190
00:10:58.708 --> 00:11:00.458
<b>Think about it</b>

191
00:11:00.458 --> 00:11:01.791
<b>- a boatman,</b>

192
00:11:01.791 --> 00:11:05.916
<b>helps others cross the river, assists them.</b>

193
00:11:05.916 --> 00:11:07.083
<b>A tailor</b>

194
00:11:07.083 --> 00:11:09.166
<b>stitches clothes for others,</b>

195
00:11:09.166 --> 00:11:11.541
<b>which gives them joy.</b>

196
00:11:11.541 --> 00:11:13.041
<b>An artist,</b>

197
00:11:13.041 --> 00:11:17.666
<b>by giving a few moments of </b>
<b>entertainment to people, removes their sorrow.</b>

198
00:11:17.666 --> 00:11:24.625
<b>The happiness and welfare of </b>
<b>others is hidden in everyone's work.</b>

199
00:11:24.625 --> 00:11:27.791
<b>By renouncing attachment to the fruit, </b>

200
00:11:27.791 --> 00:11:36.000
<b>you have to understand, </b>
<b>that how your work helps others,</b>

201
00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.583
<b>to make this help itself your purpose.</b>

202
00:11:40.583 --> 00:11:46.583
<b>To selflessly dedicate one's labor for others.</b>

203
00:11:46.583 --> 00:11:51.125
<b>This too is a kind of Yagya.</b>

204
00:11:51.125 --> 00:11:59.000
<b>A Yagya that is capable of freeing </b>
<b>you from the bondage of karma.</b>

205
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.250
<b>The only requirement is</b>

206
00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:03.791
<b>that you renounce the craving for fruit.</b>

207
00:12:03.791 --> 00:12:10.083
<b>And see your actions only from </b>
<b>the perspective of helping others.</b>

208
00:12:10.083 --> 00:12:12.166
<b>Whatever result is obtained,</b>

209
00:12:12.166 --> 00:12:15.833
<b>do not consider it your right,</b>

210
00:12:15.833 --> 00:12:21.375
<b>consider it as an offering by God,</b>

211
00:12:21.375 --> 00:12:25.666
<b>accept it in this way.</b>

212
00:12:25.666 --> 00:12:27.000
<b>Think about it.</b>

